# Qualification layer over the current local legacy controller. This does not
# replace the canonical distribution build or enable v2 in a running service.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.19 as the last installed
# native author/Red/review-launch rollback while the revision successor qualifies.
# Also retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.25, the last installed
# controller before the qualified review-stop successor; an uninstalled build
# must not displace this known operational rollback during image retirement.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.28 until the capacity-failure
# successor is natively qualified; build tags alone do not prove installed age.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.29 as the installed rollback
# until the paging/failed-inspection successor is qualified in the native flow.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.30 as the installed rollback
# while first-request review guidance and its successor are being qualified.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.31 as the installed rollback
# while the pending-page successor is qualified; do not overwrite its image tag.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.32 as the installed rollback
# until whole-page aggregate transport qualifies; historical reviews stay blocked.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.33 as the installed rollback
# while phase-specific verdict diagnostics qualify; no previous approval is inferred.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.34 as the installed rollback
# while premature-completion continuation is qualified independently.
# Retain delivery-kit-quality-v2-controller:20261023.35 as the installed rollback
# while operator-confirmed payment recovery is qualified without provider calls.
